      "writtenOn": "2025-03-18T16:12:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this would work better if you used the device variants compiled for arm64 to combine with the host code.  You can see how we do that for Java code [here](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/java/device_host_converter.go), and an example of its is usage [here](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:development/build/Android.bp;l\u003d161;drc\u003dd5b42c1f5bccdac42be2ae134b089bdd2814be78).  A similar approach should work for native code, especially if you can limit it to simple modules like cc_object or cc_genrule.",
      "parentUuid": "0c558f67_66e69605",
      "revId": "99fd863014bffe145d795858c4a5c01a5d44e47c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
